# Decided
- Links added by script (scratchpad builtin_links.py, adapted from the
  schema round's links.py to match structs too), on every overload:
  dbstat.h (dbstat, using_dbstat, make_dbstat_table: dbstat.html),
  fts5.h (fts5, using_fts5 x3: fts5.html), generate_series.h
  (generate_series, make_generate_series_table: series.html),
  pragma_table_info.h (table_info: #pragma_table_info, table_xinfo:
  #pragma_table_xinfo, make_pragma_tables: #pragfunc), rtree.h
  (using_rtree x2: rtree.html, using_rtree_i32 x2:
  #integer_valued_r_trees), sqlite_schema.h (sqlite_master;
  make_sqlite_schema_table, which had no doc-comment: schematab.html).
  Every anchor checked against the pages read 2026-11-13.
- The reflecting using_rtree/using_rtree_i32 overloads are public
  (SQLITE_ORM_EXPORT), unlike schema/'s internal reflecting factories,
  so they take the link.
- Left out: the FTS5 auxiliary functions, which link already on every
  overload (Claude's first scan miscounted them); vfs.h's name constants
  (constants, not named in decision 6); the table-reference constants
  (dbstat_table, generate_series_table, ...).

